<p>While most release their yearly review sometime in the period over Christmas - New Year’s, I figured I would be the weird one and post it the first week of January. I’ve always been the weird one.</p>
<p>2024 was a great year for me and my family, we spent the entire summer on the West Coast of Canada, flew 11 hours with our 18 month old to Italy to visit Rebecca’s extended family, I built 3 different projects to monetization, learned an immense amount about systems architecture, and didn’t sacrifice my health at the forefront of all of this.</p>
<p>While the days felt long, the year was short.  It felt like things started accelerating around September and here we are, already in 2025!</p>
